@startuml
title Sequence Diagram: Log Expense (MVVM Architecture)
autonumber

note top
    Joseph — Sprint 2
    Tracking how a lunch expense gets logged in the system
end note

' MVVM Lifelines with actual project classes
actor User
participant ExpenseLog as "ExpenseLogFragment\n(View/Fragment)"
participant ExpenseVM as "ExpenseViewModel\n(ViewModel)"
participant BudgetVM as "BudgetViewModel\n(ViewModel)"
participant ExpenseRepo as "ExpenseRepository\n(Repository)"
participant Firestore as "FirestoreManager\n(Data Layer)"
participant ExpenseModel as "Expense\n(Model)"

' === Initial Setup ===
User -> ExpenseLog: taps "Add Expense" button
activate ExpenseLog
ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: showExpenseDialog()
note right: A fresh dialog pops up,\nready for input

' Observe current date from ViewModel
ExpenseLog -> ExpenseVM: observeCurrentDate()
activate ExpenseVM
ExpenseVM -> ExpenseVM: _currentDate.value
ExpenseVM --> ExpenseLog: LiveData<LocalDate>
deactivate ExpenseVM
ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: updateDatePicker(date)

' === User Input Phase ===
User -> ExpenseLog: fills in amount, category,\ndescription, date
note left
    Sarah types in her lunch details:
    • Amount: $45.50
    • Category: "Food"
    • Description: "Lunch with the team"
    • Date: today's date
end note

' === Validation & Save ===
User -> ExpenseLog: presses "Save"
activate ExpenseLog

loop for each input field
    ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: validateInput(field)
end

alt validation fails
    ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: showError("Please fill all required fields")
    ExpenseLog --> User: displays error message
    note right: Oops! Missing fields get\nhighlighted in red
else validation succeeds
    
    ' Create expense model
    ExpenseLog -> ExpenseModel: new Expense(amount, category,\ndescription, date, userId)
    activate ExpenseModel
    ExpenseModel --> ExpenseLog: expense object
    deactivate ExpenseModel
    
    ' Pass to ViewModel
    ExpenseLog -> ExpenseVM: addExpense(expense)
    activate ExpenseVM
    
    ExpenseVM -> ExpenseRepo: saveExpense(expense)
    activate ExpenseRepo
    
    ' Repository interacts with Firestore
    ExpenseRepo -> Firestore: getInstance()
    activate Firestore
    Firestore --> ExpenseRepo: firestoreManager
    
    ExpenseRepo -> Firestore: addExpense(expense)
    Firestore -> Firestore: getDb().collection("expenses").add(expenseMap)
    
    alt Firestore success
        Firestore --> ExpenseRepo: Task<DocumentReference>
        ExpenseRepo -> ExpenseRepo: updateExpenseId(documentId)
        ExpenseRepo --> ExpenseVM: Result.Success(expense)
        deactivate Firestore
        deactivate ExpenseRepo
        
        ' Update LiveData
        ExpenseVM -> ExpenseVM: _expenses.postValue(updatedList)
        ExpenseVM -> ExpenseVM: _addExpenseResult.postValue(Success)
        ExpenseVM --> ExpenseLog: LiveData<Result>
        deactivate ExpenseVM
        
        ' Update UI
        ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: observeAddResult()
        ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: dismissDialog()
        ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: showSuccess("Expense saved!")
        ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: refreshExpenseList()
        
        ' Notify other ViewModels
        opt update budget totals
            ExpenseLog -> BudgetVM: notifyExpenseChanged()
            activate BudgetVM
            BudgetVM -> BudgetVM: recalculateTotals()
            BudgetVM -> BudgetVM: _totalSpent.postValue(newTotal)
            BudgetVM --> ExpenseLog: updates observers
            deactivate BudgetVM
            note right: Budget automatically updates\nto reflect new spending
        end
        
    else Firestore failure
        Firestore --> ExpenseRepo: Task<Exception>
        activate Firestore
        activate ExpenseRepo
        ExpenseRepo --> ExpenseVM: Result.Error(exception)
        deactivate Firestore
        deactivate ExpenseRepo
        activate ExpenseVM
        ExpenseVM -> ExpenseVM: _addExpenseResult.postValue(Error)
        ExpenseVM --> ExpenseLog: LiveData<Result.Error>
        deactivate ExpenseVM
        
        ExpenseLog -> ExpenseLog: showError("Failed to save.\nPlease try again.")
        note right: Something went wrong with\nthe network — user can retry
    end
    
end

deactivate ExpenseLog

' === Final State ===
ExpenseLog --> User: returns to expense list\nwith new expense visible

note bottom
    Architecture Overview:
    • Fragment handles UI and user interactions
    • ViewModel manages business logic and data state
    • Repository coordinates data operations
    • Firestore provides cloud persistence
    • Model represents expense data structure
end note

@enduml
